<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,061,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,061,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 01/15/97    01/08/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,061,000  30,479,000    27,204,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 265,796     163,820	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	27,730,360  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   01/15/97    01/08/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,420,000   5,399,000     4,614,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,837,000   4,968,000     4,424,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,103,000   5,174,000     4,815,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,196,000   3,326,000     2,798,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,058,000   4,146,000     3,404,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,259,000   5,376,000     5,162,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,187,000   2,090,000     1,987,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,061,000  30,479,000    27,204,000</p>
